- Relacionar os conteúdos tratados em Biologia 2 (Zoologia e Sistemas) com os conteúdos previstos no currículo de Ciências da Natureza da Educação Básica;
-  Análise crítica de kits experimentais com conteúdo de Biologia dirigidos para o ensino de Ciências da Natureza da Educação Básica;
- Elaboração de plano de aula para Ciências da Natureza das séries finais do ensino fundamental que contemple os conteúdos tratados em Biologia 2.
For each topic studied, the historical aspect will be addressed according to its relevance within the historical development of biology.
Introduction to the Animal Kingdom.
Systematics and general characteristics of animals:
- Poriferans, cnidarians, platyhelminths, nematodes, annelids, mollusks, arthropods, echinoderms, and chordates;
- The main parasites of humans and domestic animals: transmission, life cycle/vectors, and epidemiology;
- Comparative Animal Anatomy and Physiology;
- Sensory organs (hearing, balance, vision, touch, smell, and taste);
- Cardiovascular and respiratory systems;
- Digestive system;
- Excretory and Endocrine systems;
- Male and female reproductive systems.
Activities designed to connect theory with teaching practice, including:
- Relating the content covered in Biology 2 (Zoology and Systems) to the topics outlined in the Natural Sciences curriculum of Basic Education;
- Critical analysis of experimental kits with Biology content aimed at teaching Natural Sciences in Basic Education;
- Preparation of a lesson plan for Natural Sciences in the final years of elementary education that includes the content addressed in Biology 2.

